From f172a5c8280b51805f266787713a6653d304ebd8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NeoTech <andreas@roughedge.se>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 17:52:21 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] fix(app): refuse a drill R plane below the unfaced stock
 top by name

An axial drill whose R plane (Top of Part Z) lay under the declared stock
top generated clean and posted silently (G81/G73 R20 under a Z25 stock top,
and the expanded G00 Z+20 chain): drill_reach clipped the stock to R and
verify's rapid law skips every vertical rapid, so the rapid down to R
through uncut stock reached the post - a collision.

drill_reach now refuses, per cycle, any raw stock above the R plane over
the tool's body disk, by name, and the reach and holder laws read the
stock unclipped. Faced stock still counts at its raw height until #89.
Fixtures whose own declared stock stood over their R plane (lathe axial
drill, the Z-only cross file test) now sit their stock or R honestly; the
lathe golden is unchanged. The verify-side net is held as #96.

Fixes #91

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
