From c6c7bb969ddf1485a1b13dacdb8e3842304222c8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NeoTech <andreas@roughedge.se>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 18:11:17 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] fix(app): drill R-plane review fixes - part as material,
 plane max over the disk

- The R-plane law reads the part (its facets over the body disk and the
  hole's entry surface) together with the stock: with no stock, or the
  stock as the op's source, it no longer gets an empty slice - a
  stockless R under the part top is refused, naming "the part top".
- A facet counts at its plane's maximum over the disk (clipped to the
  circumscribing octagon), not its highest vertex: a drafted stock top
  no longer refuses an honest R or names the far vertex's height. The
  reach and holder laws share the reader. The readers move to
  operation/drill_top.rs (drill_reach under 400 lines).
- Seeding unchanged (Top of Stock has no stockless fallback and the seed
  has no world); the UX cost recorded in RECOMMENDED.md.
- drill_rplane: the post-path refusal asserts its words; Spot/Tap/Bore,
  a hole beside the stock footprint, R from Top of Stock, stockless and
  drafted cases added. drilling_cross's Z-only fixture asserts Ok.
  operations' staleness fixture moved the part up under its fixed R (a
  real refusal now); it moves down instead.

Refs #91

